Asynchronous event handling
As we mentioned earlier, if the chain of calls demand asynchronous execution, the async
chain should in fact be propagated all the way to the top of the call hierarchy. Deviating
from this setup may cause threading issues, race conditions, and possibly deadlocks.
Nevertheless, it is also important that the methods should not deviate from the async Task
declaration, ensuring that the async stack and generated results and errors are preserved.
